{
  "info": {
    "name": "Portfolio v2.0 API",
    "description": "Full backend API. Suggested order: run folders top to bottom (0 through 6). Requests are numbered within each folder in the order they make sense to run.\n\nBEFORE YOU START\n1. npm run seed in server/ - creates SUPER_ADMIN + sample ADMIN + 2 AUTHORs.\n2. npm run dev in server/ - starts the API on http://localhost:5000.\n3. Open the collection variables and fill in the real email/password values - they're placeholders below, not committed anywhere.\n\nCOOKIES AND CSRF\nAuth is two cookies, not a bearer token: auth_token (httpOnly) and csrf_token (readable). Your client must send cookies automatically (default in Postman/Requestly for same-domain requests) AND echo csrf_token back as the x-csrf-token header on every POST/PATCH/DELETE. Every Login request here has a test script that reads the csrf_token cookie and stores it in {{csrfToken}}, which the header on mutating requests references automatically. If your client doesn't run test scripts, copy the csrf_token cookie value into the csrfToken variable by hand.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5000/api/v1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "csrfToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "superAdminEmail",
      "value": "REPLACE_WITH_SEED_SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "superAdminPassword",
      "value": "REPLACE_WITH_SEED_SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "admin@example.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "author1Email",
      "value": "author1@example.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "author2Email",
      "value": "author2@example.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "samplePassword",
      "value": "REPLACE_WITH_SEED_SAMPLE_PASSWORD",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "categoryId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "categoryChildId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "categorySlug",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "tagId1",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "tagId2",
      "value": "",
